1
00:02:04,780 --> 00:02:08,780
NO ANIMALS WERE HARMED DURING
THE FILMING OF THIS PRODUCTION

2
00:02:10,590 --> 00:02:25,340
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

3
00:02:28,550 --> 00:02:33,030
Genghis Khan Laws say ''If you are served
a beverage at the lands of your enemy...

4
00:02:33,030 --> 00:02:37,940
...you should always make sure it's
not poisoned.''

5
00:02:56,800 --> 00:02:59,010
One way or another you will get to taste
it.

6
00:02:59,960 --> 00:03:02,320
We will have a feast the day you die.

7
00:03:09,100 --> 00:03:09,860
Let her go!

8
00:03:10,620 --> 00:03:11,660
You bloodless.

9
00:03:13,990 --> 00:03:14,690
Aunt!

10
00:03:18,670 --> 00:03:19,760
No! Don't do it!

11
00:03:20,770 --> 00:03:21,850
Let her go!

12
00:03:22,280 --> 00:03:23,340
Let them go!

13
00:03:26,300 --> 00:03:27,150
Balgay!

14
00:03:27,850 --> 00:03:29,890
You tormented us enough already!

15
00:03:30,090 --> 00:03:34,570
Nobody can question me and my people.

16
00:03:34,890 --> 00:03:38,530
Who do you think you are?
You sneaky rat.

17
00:03:47,620 --> 00:03:49,040
Let Selcan Hatun go!

18
00:03:49,640 --> 00:03:51,140
You are going to kill her!

19
00:03:59,310 --> 00:04:00,920
Please! Let her go!

20
00:04:01,220 --> 00:04:02,300
It's enough I said!

21
00:04:02,310 --> 00:04:03,550
Can't you understand?

22
00:04:05,380 --> 00:04:06,180
Enough!

23
00:04:12,620 --> 00:04:13,320
My Valiants!

24
00:04:13,760 --> 00:04:14,470
My brothers!

25
00:04:15,740 --> 00:04:16,720
The duty calls us.

26
00:04:16,880 --> 00:04:18,690
Our swords will say the last words!

27
00:04:21,010 --> 00:04:22,730
Are we going to wait for Osman Bey?

28
00:04:23,340 --> 00:04:25,720
My sweet child, we can wait but there is
one thing.

29
00:04:25,720 --> 00:04:27,210
The enemy will not wait.

30
00:04:29,720 --> 00:04:30,750
Another thing.

31
00:04:30,920 --> 00:04:31,640
Bala Hatun.

32
00:04:32,650 --> 00:04:33,690
Gonca Hatun.

33
00:04:34,030 --> 00:04:35,790
You should tell Sheikh Edebali...

34
00:04:35,790 --> 00:04:38,480
...that we are about to fight our foes.

35
00:04:39,540 --> 00:04:40,770
Tell him exactly that...

36
00:04:40,990 --> 00:04:44,180
If the warriors of Kayı come back, they
will do so as war veterans.

37
00:04:44,180 --> 00:04:46,410
If they will not survive, however, as
martyrs.

38
00:04:46,410 --> 00:04:47,740
Let his prayers be with us.

39
00:04:50,430 --> 00:04:51,290
Farewell.

40
00:05:15,250 --> 00:05:18,190
I will gouge out your eyes so that you
will understand...

41
00:05:18,190 --> 00:05:20,910
...what mixing my beverage with poison
means.

42
00:05:31,260 --> 00:05:31,990
Enough!

43
00:05:33,070 --> 00:05:35,230
Is your power enough only for a Hatun?

44
00:05:35,270 --> 00:05:36,010
You dog!

45
00:05:40,850 --> 00:05:41,600
Gündüz!

46
00:05:42,480 --> 00:05:43,190
Gündüz!

47
00:05:44,870 --> 00:05:45,640
Balgay!

48
00:05:46,260 --> 00:05:47,090
I said enough.

49
00:05:47,440 --> 00:05:48,540
Don't you understand?

50
00:05:50,360 --> 00:05:51,080
Father!

51
00:05:51,230 --> 00:05:52,040
Dündar!

52
00:05:53,450 --> 00:05:54,360
Gündüz!

53
00:05:54,360 --> 00:05:56,520
My Allah please help us.

54
00:06:01,650 --> 00:06:02,880
Let my father go!

55
00:06:04,090 --> 00:06:04,820
Father!

56
00:06:04,840 --> 00:06:05,550
Father!

57
00:06:07,010 --> 00:06:09,250
Shepherd's dog, oh shepherd's dog,

58
00:06:09,730 --> 00:06:13,730
Who will guard the sheep if you also die
now?

59
00:06:15,180 --> 00:06:16,970
Please let him go!

60
00:06:44,750 --> 00:06:47,510
Today is the day Ahis and Gaziyans work
side by side.

61
00:06:48,560 --> 00:06:51,380
You should urgently go to my father
and tell him everything.

62
00:06:52,020 --> 00:06:52,750
You?

63
00:06:52,950 --> 00:06:54,910
We should find out more.

64
00:06:55,620 --> 00:06:56,780
I will stay here.

65
00:06:59,280 --> 00:07:00,730
May Allah be with you.

66
00:07:01,660 --> 00:07:02,880
You too, Gonca.

67
00:07:52,670 --> 00:07:53,420
Mother!

68
00:08:06,030 --> 00:08:07,330
Honorable enemies...

69
00:08:07,910 --> 00:08:09,390
...should not die like
insects.

70
00:08:10,400 --> 00:08:14,400
Osman once said his root goes back all way
to Oguz Khan.

71
00:08:15,960 --> 00:08:18,090
In Mongol traditions, relatives of Khan...

72
00:08:18,410 --> 00:08:21,220
...get tied up to be chewed by
the horses.

73
00:08:23,800 --> 00:08:26,480
Because we think bad luck will come...

74
00:08:26,480 --> 00:08:28,800
...if their blood spills on our land.

75
00:08:32,650 --> 00:08:34,690
Take these ones to jail.

76
00:08:36,520 --> 00:08:37,370
Brother!

77
00:08:38,530 --> 00:08:39,400
My son!

78
00:08:40,540 --> 00:08:41,580
Leave me alone!

79
00:08:41,600 --> 00:08:43,140
I said leave me alone!

80
00:08:50,830 --> 00:08:53,580
I will hunt the herd.

81
00:08:54,660 --> 00:08:57,980
While shepherd's dog Dündar watches me
doing it.

82
00:09:02,860 --> 00:09:03,690
Brother!

83
00:09:05,390 --> 00:09:06,180
Ayşe!

84
00:09:06,400 --> 00:09:06,910
Ayşe!

85
00:09:21,140 --> 00:09:22,260
Now!

86
00:09:22,980 --> 00:09:25,610
All of you will see what happens when
you don't obey...

87
00:09:26,230 --> 00:09:27,960
...the commands of Mongols.

88
00:09:30,020 --> 00:09:30,990
Don't touch me.

89
00:09:30,990 --> 00:09:33,040
To die is to meet my Rab for me.

90
00:09:33,050 --> 00:09:34,810
I will die with my honor.

91
00:09:35,440 --> 00:09:36,650
Let me go!

92
00:09:39,700 --> 00:09:40,600
Gündüz Bey!

93
00:09:42,450 --> 00:09:43,280
Gündüz!

94
00:09:43,720 --> 00:09:44,750
Gündüz Bey!

95
00:09:48,870 --> 00:09:49,640
My son!

96
00:09:50,950 --> 00:09:51,720
Batur Bey!

97
00:10:02,080 --> 00:10:04,540
My Allah, please don't test me with child
loss.

98
00:10:05,840 --> 00:10:06,540
Balgay.

99
00:10:06,540 --> 00:10:08,790
You tortured us enough already, I said.

100
00:10:10,440 --> 00:10:12,370
It's time, my sons!

101
00:10:13,080 --> 00:10:13,930
Come on!

102
00:10:28,790 --> 00:10:29,670
My friends!

103
00:10:33,960 --> 00:10:34,750
My frıends!

104
00:10:39,280 --> 00:10:41,940
The Shahada time has come!

105
00:10:44,830 --> 00:10:46,370
The time...

106
00:10:46,370 --> 00:10:47,780
...of clash is also here!

107
00:10:52,020 --> 00:10:53,880
Allahu akbar!

108
00:11:01,200 --> 00:11:02,540
Allahu akbar!

109
00:11:34,600 --> 00:11:35,300
Bala!

110
00:11:43,940 --> 00:11:45,480
Allahu akbar!

111
00:12:04,220 --> 00:12:06,360
Tell your people to stop right there.

112
00:12:14,720 --> 00:12:15,860
My kin!

113
00:12:16,870 --> 00:12:18,420
We can't be defeated!

114
00:12:19,650 --> 00:12:20,820
Arm your swords!

115
00:12:22,810 --> 00:12:25,330
Playing the mute devil does not exist in
our culture!

116
00:12:32,490 --> 00:12:33,340
The time...

117
00:12:41,420 --> 00:12:42,760
of Shahada is here!

118
00:12:43,020 --> 00:12:44,130
Allahu Akbar!

119
00:12:48,630 --> 00:12:49,700
Allahu Akbar!

120
00:12:57,010 --> 00:12:58,330
Allahu Akbar!

121
00:13:07,990 --> 00:13:08,730
Osman.

122
00:13:16,230 --> 00:13:17,250
Brother.

123
00:13:21,830 --> 00:13:23,740
My Osman has arrived.

124
00:13:23,970 --> 00:13:25,710
Your power is unquestionable my Rab.

125
00:13:25,990 --> 00:13:26,940
Thank you.

126
00:13:52,720 --> 00:13:53,630
Balgay!

127
00:13:54,210 --> 00:13:58,210
Welcome to Balgay's Hell, Osman.

128
00:13:58,990 --> 00:14:00,980
I came here to clean our Tents.

129
00:14:05,410 --> 00:14:06,700
You and your men...

130
00:14:07,890 --> 00:14:09,770
...better stop this persecution.

131
00:14:11,920 --> 00:14:15,920
Do you know what I see when I look at you?

132
00:14:17,530 --> 00:14:21,530
A carcass that is chopped into pieces
to feed the hounds.

133
00:14:22,550 --> 00:14:24,770
That's your reflection on
the mirror, Balgay.

134
00:14:27,980 --> 00:14:29,870
I offered you bannerlordship...

135
00:14:30,760 --> 00:14:32,000
...but you refused.

136
00:14:36,530 --> 00:14:38,370
Then, I told you I'll be your death.

137
00:14:39,920 --> 00:14:42,520
A word leaves my mouth only once.

138
00:14:42,860 --> 00:14:44,930
I always keep my promises, Osman Bey.

139
00:14:45,440 --> 00:14:47,480
You are dead now!

140
00:14:50,700 --> 00:14:52,550
I came here not to obey...

141
00:14:56,470 --> 00:14:58,670
...but to give you the might of Genghis
Khan.

142
00:15:19,410 --> 00:15:21,820
The might of Genghis Khan is not a joke.

143
00:15:23,050 --> 00:15:25,210
What might are you talking about?

144
00:15:26,410 --> 00:15:28,430
Now, you'll either listen to me...

145
00:15:29,640 --> 00:15:33,520
...or lose your luck.

146
00:15:38,330 --> 00:15:42,330
I have a treasure no Mongol commander can
reject.

147
00:15:53,480 --> 00:15:57,640
While the might of Genghis Khan flows in
my noble veins...

148
00:15:57,640 --> 00:16:00,230
...how do you dare to talk like this?

149
00:16:00,590 --> 00:16:02,910
Genghis Khan says...

150
00:16:02,940 --> 00:16:04,710
...listen to your enemy well when...

151
00:16:04,710 --> 00:16:08,090
...he stands in front you with consent
and courage.

152
00:16:08,650 --> 00:16:09,620
So that...

153
00:16:11,310 --> 00:16:15,310
...you can prove you are as valiant your
enemy.

154
00:16:28,520 --> 00:16:29,410
Or else...

155
00:16:30,010 --> 00:16:32,960
...are you telling me that you are not
courages enough, Balgay?

156
00:17:00,150 --> 00:17:02,130
Commander Balgay.

157
00:17:02,650 --> 00:17:04,480
Emissaries from Konya are approaching.

158
00:17:05,880 --> 00:17:08,100
These are the ones Geyhatu sent before.

159
00:17:32,140 --> 00:17:34,790
You have news from Geyhatu, Balgay.

160
00:18:19,970 --> 00:18:21,760
Geyhatu wants you.

161
00:18:22,620 --> 00:18:25,330
He wants me to send your Alps to Konya.

162
00:18:30,460 --> 00:18:32,200
How did you meet Geyhatu?

163
00:18:33,050 --> 00:18:34,800
What are you up to, Osman?

164
00:18:40,400 --> 00:18:42,820
Geyhatu appreciates the treasure I know.

165
00:18:43,790 --> 00:18:45,940
I have been waiting for him.

166
00:18:48,620 --> 00:18:51,320
What is that treasure Geyhatu wants to
posses so much?

167
00:19:58,560 --> 00:20:00,430
What are you up to, Osman?

168
00:20:00,610 --> 00:20:01,560
Hush, Hatun.

169
00:20:01,790 --> 00:20:02,540
Hush!

170
00:20:03,560 --> 00:20:04,990
He knows what is doing.

171
00:20:10,320 --> 00:20:11,070
Soldiers!

172
00:20:11,630 --> 00:20:12,760
Put your swords down.

173
00:20:28,570 --> 00:20:29,280
Tonga!

174
00:20:29,410 --> 00:20:30,140
Cankutay!

175
00:20:30,690 --> 00:20:31,810
Stop the executions!

176
00:20:32,470 --> 00:20:33,360
Take the captives.

177
00:20:33,870 --> 00:20:35,240
It is an order from Geyhatu.

178
00:21:09,200 --> 00:21:09,920
What happened?

179
00:21:09,920 --> 00:21:11,340
Don't care about that.

180
00:21:12,500 --> 00:21:14,390
Osman ruined all of our plans.

181
00:21:14,910 --> 00:21:16,870
He wasted Alişar and Balgay.

182
00:21:17,110 --> 00:21:18,580
He got Nizamettin killed.

183
00:21:19,360 --> 00:21:20,190
And now, Balgay.

184
00:21:22,080 --> 00:21:22,830
Mongols!

185
00:21:25,470 --> 00:21:27,320
They came to our land, along with...

186
00:21:28,440 --> 00:21:30,090
their bad smell and greed.

187
00:21:32,110 --> 00:21:34,800
You can have the same enemy with Mongols.

188
00:21:34,800 --> 00:21:37,080
But you should never be friends with them.

189
00:21:37,080 --> 00:21:38,080
My daughter.

190
00:21:38,250 --> 00:21:39,600
Curse be upon them.

191
00:21:40,810 --> 00:21:44,240
We should no longer expect anything from
Balgay the Uncivilized.

192
00:21:47,160 --> 00:21:48,950
I had kiss his dirty hands.

193
00:21:51,000 --> 00:21:53,520
The more I think of it, the more I get
disgusted.

194
00:21:54,340 --> 00:21:56,110
Balgay is an absolute trouble.

195
00:21:56,630 --> 00:21:59,000
He neither gets anything nor listens to
us.

196
00:22:00,230 --> 00:22:02,800
However, he is not our only hope.

197
00:22:04,490 --> 00:22:07,010
There may be another way to our salvation.

198
00:22:10,180 --> 00:22:11,460
Salvador!

199
00:22:16,050 --> 00:22:18,270
Can we trust Salvador, master?

200
00:22:18,870 --> 00:22:20,600
He might play a double game.

201
00:22:20,600 --> 00:22:22,320
We can't know without trying, Sofia.

202
00:22:23,230 --> 00:22:23,940
We will try.

203
00:22:24,510 --> 00:22:27,460
Both Salvador and the Mongols.

204
00:22:28,350 --> 00:22:30,360
Remember the person you know the best...

205
00:22:31,350 --> 00:22:33,760
...is your partner crime, Princess.

206
00:22:34,390 --> 00:22:35,820
And, I know Mongols the best.

207
00:22:37,240 --> 00:22:39,240
We will present Constantinople to them.

208
00:22:41,500 --> 00:22:43,610
They are powerful enough to take it.

209
00:22:44,220 --> 00:22:47,930
In this way, you will be the Queen.

210
00:22:47,930 --> 00:22:50,250
And one day, you will be very surprised
when...

211
00:22:50,250 --> 00:22:53,240
...your Mongol King dies all of a sudden.

212
00:23:03,040 --> 00:23:05,820
You are coming to my Tent, Osman Bey,

213
00:23:09,910 --> 00:23:11,780
We need to talk somewhere private.

214
00:23:37,030 --> 00:23:39,060
You may come with us, Dündar Bey.

215
00:23:56,420 --> 00:23:58,630
What are you talking about Osman?

216
00:23:58,630 --> 00:24:00,680
What does ''the Might of Genghis Khan"
mean?

217
00:24:00,680 --> 00:24:03,030
I won't let them hurt our people, uncle.

218
00:24:10,760 --> 00:24:12,080
You should trust me.

219
00:25:19,040 --> 00:25:21,530
You must be respectful in front of Balgay.
You, Turk!

220
00:25:43,870 --> 00:25:45,540
I want to learn what he has to say.

221
00:25:54,700 --> 00:25:56,710
I am not here for childish games, Balgay.

222
00:26:07,510 --> 00:26:09,760
Think twice before you talk.

223
00:26:10,430 --> 00:26:11,850
Stop messing around.

224
00:26:11,850 --> 00:26:12,580
I am listening.

225
00:26:12,580 --> 00:26:13,350
Speak!

226
00:26:14,750 --> 00:26:16,350
I don't take orders from Mongols.

227
00:26:21,580 --> 00:26:22,290
Uncle!

228
00:26:28,660 --> 00:26:30,080
What's the matter, son?

229
00:26:56,190 --> 00:26:59,450
Is this dagger I'm holding right now...

230
00:27:01,240 --> 00:27:02,260
..."Law Defender"?

231
00:27:05,920 --> 00:27:07,440
It's the exact dagger...

232
00:27:07,440 --> 00:27:09,930
...that defended Genghis Khan's laws.

233
00:27:38,400 --> 00:27:39,750
He lost his mind.

234
00:27:43,330 --> 00:27:47,100
My Bey came here to bring us salvation.

235
00:27:47,100 --> 00:27:47,810
Praise him!

236
00:27:50,930 --> 00:27:54,930
I was a captive some time ago.

237
00:27:56,190 --> 00:27:59,250
Ertugrul Bey saved me as fast as he could.

238
00:28:01,960 --> 00:28:02,700
My brothers!

239
00:28:04,830 --> 00:28:08,830
We will not let them survive on these
lands.

240
00:28:13,710 --> 00:28:16,510
The situation is different this time
Valiants.

241
00:28:18,350 --> 00:28:20,660
I saw so many Mongols in my life.

242
00:28:22,290 --> 00:28:25,100
However, Balgay is different...

243
00:28:25,100 --> 00:28:27,350
...and stronger than the rest of them.

244
00:28:29,870 --> 00:28:33,970
In order to remain the one and only rulers
of these lands.

245
00:28:33,970 --> 00:28:35,380
To defeat him.

246
00:28:35,380 --> 00:28:37,960
You should also trick him and make plans.

247
00:28:41,570 --> 00:28:46,430
Once we are free, if I can't teach
them some lessons.

248
00:28:46,430 --> 00:28:49,290
If I can't make them learn about how to
respect us.

249
00:28:49,290 --> 00:28:53,290
I will not be able to feel like a soldier
anymore.

250
00:29:06,830 --> 00:29:08,150
Where did you find this?

251
00:29:11,380 --> 00:29:12,770
Commander Balgay.

252
00:29:12,770 --> 00:29:14,140
Osman is lying.

253
00:29:15,590 --> 00:29:18,320
A Turk couldn't posses the mighty
dagger of Genghis Khan.

254
00:29:24,150 --> 00:29:24,880
Balgay!

255
00:29:26,880 --> 00:29:29,310
It seems like you could not raise your
men properly.

256
00:29:30,410 --> 00:29:31,900
They question your authority.

257
00:29:38,890 --> 00:29:40,960
If all of your men are like these two.

258
00:29:41,660 --> 00:29:44,080
You won't be able to conquer
Constantinople.

259
00:30:18,610 --> 00:30:23,670
Take all the bounties to your people and
punish your enemies.

260
00:30:40,660 --> 00:30:42,530
Law Defender.

261
00:30:44,780 --> 00:30:48,780
I have the Laws of Genghis Khan...

262
00:30:49,610 --> 00:30:52,710
...written by Şigi Kutugu

263
00:30:59,960 --> 00:31:03,700
Do you have the forgotten laws of mighty
Genghis Khan?

264
00:31:08,570 --> 00:31:10,830
Do you have any idea what that means?

265
00:31:15,840 --> 00:31:16,730
Where is it?

266
00:31:16,730 --> 00:31:18,180
Hand it to me at once!

267
00:31:18,680 --> 00:31:20,190
Only under some conditions.

268
00:31:20,940 --> 00:31:22,140
Tell me right now!

269
00:31:24,250 --> 00:31:25,360
You will free my Alps.

270
00:31:26,210 --> 00:31:27,680
You will leave our lands.

271
00:31:31,390 --> 00:31:33,580
You will give our golds back.

272
00:31:36,560 --> 00:31:40,560
And you will promise in front of all Beys.

273
00:31:54,640 --> 00:31:55,640
I came here...

274
00:31:58,710 --> 00:32:02,400
...to kill those who try to rise
against me.

275
00:32:06,710 --> 00:32:10,180
If the things you say are not true...

276
00:32:10,180 --> 00:32:16,460
...I will destroy the Kayı Tent with my
army today.

277
00:32:18,070 --> 00:32:19,970
Just for your information.

278
00:32:29,000 --> 00:32:30,140
May our sorrow end.

279
00:32:31,290 --> 00:32:32,330
May we break free.

280
00:32:35,070 --> 00:32:36,630
May the gates of heaven be open.

281
00:32:43,220 --> 00:32:46,460
i seek protection in Allah
from the accursed shaytan.

282
00:32:46,820 --> 00:32:50,180
In the name of Allah,
the Beneficent, the Merciful

283
00:32:51,340 --> 00:32:55,740
Indeed, We have given you,
[O Muhammad], a clear conquest
Surah Al-Fath [48]

284
00:32:56,380 --> 00:33:04,380
That Allah may forgive for you
what preceded of your sin

285
00:33:05,060 --> 00:33:11,740
and what will follow and complete His favor upon you and guide you to a straight path

286
00:33:11,780 --> 00:33:15,380
And [that] Allah may aid
you with a mighty victory.

287
00:33:16,660 --> 00:33:25,660
It is He who sent down tranquillity into the hearts of the believers that they would increase in faith along with their [present] faith.

288
00:33:26,060 --> 00:33:34,300
And to Allah belong the soldiers of the heavens and the earth, and ever is Allah Knowing and Wise.
Surah Al-Fath [48]

289
00:33:36,060 --> 00:33:37,580
My Osman...

290
00:33:37,580 --> 00:33:40,230
...will not surrender to Balgay's order.

291
00:33:41,230 --> 00:33:43,540
We all need to be careful these days.

292
00:33:44,180 --> 00:33:48,540
We might have to fight our enemies any day
now. The war might be on our door.

293
00:33:49,030 --> 00:33:51,760
And this time the consequences can be
much worse, my Bey.

294
00:33:52,480 --> 00:33:54,820
As long as we are together...

295
00:33:54,830 --> 00:33:56,850
...nothing can stop us.

296
00:33:56,850 --> 00:33:59,020
All we need to do is just believe.

297
00:33:59,230 --> 00:34:03,750
We'll put it out, my lovely child.
We'll put it out.

298
00:34:07,770 --> 00:34:13,310
The treasure you have brought blessed me.

299
00:34:13,420 --> 00:34:18,210
I have come one step closer to
my ancestor Genghis' soul in the sky.

300
00:34:23,900 --> 00:34:27,230
You asked for Beys. Now they are here.

301
00:34:27,570 --> 00:34:29,630
Say what you want to say.

302
00:34:30,500 --> 00:34:34,210
We manage our Tents with laws...

303
00:34:35,420 --> 00:34:37,920
... our laws with our meetings.

304
00:34:38,230 --> 00:34:42,080
But a meeting doesn't begin this way.

305
00:35:01,120 --> 00:35:04,420
In the ninety-nine names of Allah

306
00:35:05,340 --> 00:35:08,630
who has the power to create

307
00:35:09,200 --> 00:35:12,470
and who fills our hearts with faith.

308
00:35:16,870 --> 00:35:19,100
Valiant Beys of Kayı.

309
00:35:19,100 --> 00:35:25,560
I have the Genghis' laws, which are also
valued greatly by Balgay.

310
00:35:26,410 --> 00:35:30,150
These laws are very important for
a Mongol commander.

311
00:35:32,410 --> 00:35:37,940
Because Mongols have been following
traces for these treasures.

312
00:35:38,900 --> 00:35:42,220
Now I have them.

313
00:35:47,630 --> 00:35:52,330
I'll bring those laws, and Balgay will
leave the Tent in return.

314
00:35:57,610 --> 00:35:59,750
He'll release our Alps.

315
00:36:00,480 --> 00:36:06,010
I wanted him to promise in front of you.

316
00:36:06,640 --> 00:36:08,480
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

317
00:36:32,330 --> 00:36:34,080
My ancestor Genghis!

318
00:36:34,080 --> 00:36:39,400
- speaking in Mongol -

319
00:36:42,500 --> 00:36:49,360
Watch yourself when you're alone.
Watch your word when you're not.

320
00:36:50,840 --> 00:36:52,280
He said.

321
00:36:55,480 --> 00:37:03,430
I'm Balgay. I've made my promise.
If Osman also keeps his promise...

322
00:37:05,430 --> 00:37:08,850
I swear I'll do what he said.

323
00:37:18,430 --> 00:37:20,280
But...

324
00:37:21,850 --> 00:37:25,850
If these are tricks within tricks...

325
00:37:27,870 --> 00:37:34,600
I'll burn your goats and dogs! Know that!

326
00:37:35,410 --> 00:37:40,260
I won't even let your babies live!

327
00:37:41,210 --> 00:37:42,970
Then...

328
00:37:44,850 --> 00:37:47,390
... it's my job to keep my promise.

329
00:38:25,040 --> 00:38:27,900
- Speak.
- Master...

330
00:38:27,900 --> 00:38:30,030
Osman is dangerous!

331
00:38:30,530 --> 00:38:35,990
Even if there are a lot of people
around him, he's like a lone wolf.

332
00:38:35,990 --> 00:38:40,260
It's true that he's alone.
The Mongols have all his Alps.

333
00:38:40,690 --> 00:38:44,480
Just like how he has all my soldiers.

334
00:38:46,830 --> 00:38:51,680
Let me go find out what
he's doing and where he is.

335
00:38:59,890 --> 00:39:02,260
You might be lying.

336
00:39:02,710 --> 00:39:06,290
You might fight against us
with Osman again.

337
00:39:11,490 --> 00:39:17,830
One can escape death
a lot of times, Salvador.

338
00:39:18,520 --> 00:39:22,050
But no one runs forever.

339
00:39:25,200 --> 00:39:27,430
Do you understand?

340
00:39:43,770 --> 00:39:45,430
Yes, Master.

341
00:39:47,420 --> 00:39:51,170
Trust me. I'll serve you in this battle.

342
00:39:51,780 --> 00:39:57,650
I will not die before I give you
Osman and redeem myself.

343
00:40:03,620 --> 00:40:06,880
If you make one mistake...

344
00:40:08,260 --> 00:40:12,000
... I'll skin you alive.

345
00:40:24,300 --> 00:40:29,360
My Osman! My Osman.
What did that infidel Balgay say?

346
00:40:29,380 --> 00:40:32,730
He will keep his promise, Bamsı Bey.
Don't you worry.

347
00:40:32,730 --> 00:40:36,720
He'll leave our Tent.
He'll release our Alps.

348
00:40:36,720 --> 00:40:40,780
Good, my Osman. But where did those
Genghis Khan laws come from?

349
00:40:41,330 --> 00:40:43,440
Who gave them to you, my Osman?

350
00:40:47,540 --> 00:40:49,710
It's a secret, Bamsı Bey.

351
00:40:51,680 --> 00:40:53,620
I can't say anything else.

352
00:40:53,720 --> 00:40:55,100
Son!

353
00:40:56,720 --> 00:41:00,170
How can a friend hide
something from his fellow?

354
00:41:04,950 --> 00:41:08,110
There are things friends can't do,
Bamsı Bey.

355
00:41:10,340 --> 00:41:15,060
My Osman, these lands were
empty when we came.

356
00:41:15,310 --> 00:41:19,130
We paved these roads with
our blood, our lives!

357
00:41:20,550 --> 00:41:27,420
My Osman, this situation disturbs me.
Tell me. What is the truth?

358
00:41:30,750 --> 00:41:34,070
- Don't push me, Bamsı Bey.
- Osman!

359
00:41:35,620 --> 00:41:40,440
Don't push it, Bamsı Bey!
I can't say more.

360
00:41:55,710 --> 00:41:58,810
We don't call this friendship.

361
00:42:01,670 --> 00:42:04,840
Either we were wrong...

362
00:42:06,410 --> 00:42:10,410
... or we couldn't teach you that.

363
00:42:23,290 --> 00:42:28,110
It's obvious why Geyhatu
wants Gengis' Laws from Osman, Balgay.

364
00:42:29,020 --> 00:42:33,570
Whoever has the laws,
has the power, Cerkutay.

365
00:42:35,010 --> 00:42:37,940
no one can stand in their way.

366
00:42:38,750 --> 00:42:46,460
If Osman brings the laws, you'll be
the might and the power in these lands.

367
00:42:51,150 --> 00:42:56,000
Me having them is not the point.

368
00:42:56,910 --> 00:43:06,630
How did Osman find this dagger which
was protecting Genghis Khan's laws?

369
00:43:08,440 --> 00:43:11,140
How could Geyhatu know this?

370
00:43:12,590 --> 00:43:19,920
I didn't ask Osman where he found it.
Why would he think I fell into his trap?

371
00:43:21,190 --> 00:43:28,040
I shall acquire the power first.
I'll figure it out when the time comes.

372
00:43:28,360 --> 00:43:31,430
If Osman brings the laws...

373
00:43:32,260 --> 00:43:34,400
... will you give them to Geyhatu?

374
00:43:36,140 --> 00:43:40,140
He'll take them himself. If he can.

375
00:43:43,290 --> 00:43:48,130
I'll take him to the Mongol Khanate
myself.

376
00:43:50,030 --> 00:43:55,430
Balgay will finally be in a
position he deserves!

377
00:44:13,470 --> 00:44:15,440
What's the status?

378
00:44:16,560 --> 00:44:20,570
Balgay took the bait.
I'll take care of the rest.

379
00:44:21,530 --> 00:44:28,250
Then go, my Osman! The world is yours!

380
00:44:44,720 --> 00:44:51,310
Go! The mountains, the rivers
shall follow your way!

381
00:44:59,200 --> 00:45:03,000
I never thought I'd pray for Osman.

382
00:45:03,560 --> 00:45:06,330
Poor Zöhre.

383
00:45:07,330 --> 00:45:14,330
You're relying on the mad man Osman
for your son's life.

384
00:45:14,330 --> 00:45:18,330
We're not relying on anyone, Hatun!

385
00:45:19,900 --> 00:45:23,900
Do you think I'll let that infidel
Balgay decide my son's fate?

386
00:45:24,680 --> 00:45:29,400
I'll face him if necessary, but I
won't let him touch my son!

387
00:45:29,930 --> 00:45:34,080
Watch your words!
Don't make me go mental!

388
00:45:34,500 --> 00:45:37,270
I'm worried about my son, Dündar Bey!

389
00:45:37,970 --> 00:45:41,120
I hope Osman takes care
of this as soon as possible.

390
00:45:41,280 --> 00:45:48,180
If he does, not only me, the whole Tent
will see him as a Bey.

391
00:45:48,970 --> 00:45:52,970
Instead of screaming at me, think about
what you'll do when that day comes.

392
00:45:54,900 --> 00:45:58,900
I say the last word in the Kayı Tent.

393
00:45:59,500 --> 00:46:01,870
Osman also knows this very well.

394
00:46:04,070 --> 00:46:09,950
Osman tied a knot,
he will untie it himself.

395
00:46:10,170 --> 00:46:14,460
It's not about meetings, being a Bey,
or about Bala.

396
00:46:17,950 --> 00:46:20,430
Not that much.

397
00:46:30,690 --> 00:46:33,340
They tortured you a lot, Sıddık.

398
00:46:34,160 --> 00:46:38,160
They did. But it was worth it, Osman Bey.

399
00:46:38,370 --> 00:46:41,650
Besides, is being Sıddık easy?

400
00:46:44,540 --> 00:46:47,620
Tell me. What's the status?

401
00:46:48,240 --> 00:46:53,790
I convinced Yannis and Sofia. They sent
me to gather information about you.

402
00:46:54,820 --> 00:47:00,520
Then we'll give them what they want.
So that they trust you more.

403
00:47:00,800 --> 00:47:02,850
What do you want me to say?

404
00:47:03,110 --> 00:47:07,340
Tell them I'm about to save
the Tent from Balgay.

405
00:47:08,000 --> 00:47:10,290
They will ask how.

406
00:47:10,690 --> 00:47:13,890
I have something that can excite Balgay.

407
00:47:14,990 --> 00:47:17,040
Genghis Khans' laws.

408
00:47:18,980 --> 00:47:22,550
They will worry about this.

409
00:47:22,550 --> 00:47:25,200
If they worry, they
will fall into the trap.

410
00:47:26,260 --> 00:47:29,780
Now go. Do as I say.

411
00:48:16,060 --> 00:48:21,460
You couldn't do anything to tied men.
Are you trying your luck on women now?

412
00:48:22,960 --> 00:48:24,740
Degenerate!

413
00:48:33,730 --> 00:48:35,700
Mongol dog!

414
00:48:36,260 --> 00:48:37,830
Look at me!

415
00:48:38,690 --> 00:48:42,390
What? Are you scared?

416
00:48:47,030 --> 00:48:50,070
You haven't talked since Osman Bey came.

417
00:48:53,450 --> 00:48:55,420
Don't!

418
00:48:57,440 --> 00:48:58,830
- Konur!
- Dog!

419
00:48:58,830 --> 00:49:04,250
Don't you worry.
It will be your turn soon!

420
00:49:05,300 --> 00:49:06,920
All of yours!

421
00:49:10,410 --> 00:49:14,080
Devil's son! Just wait.

422
00:49:14,860 --> 00:49:17,320
I'll strangle you myself.

423
00:49:17,990 --> 00:49:23,180
If I don't pull your flesh from
your bones, I shall not be called Konur!

424
00:49:38,990 --> 00:49:42,990
Your eyes are not slanted.

425
00:49:43,530 --> 00:49:46,910
You're not short either.

426
00:49:47,300 --> 00:49:51,900
Tell me. What did this Mongol give you
so you became his puppy?

427
00:49:57,920 --> 00:49:59,920
I see.

428
00:50:03,130 --> 00:50:05,360
You're a numbskull.

429
00:50:07,410 --> 00:50:09,370
Numbskull.

430
00:50:09,720 --> 00:50:15,860
What did you call me? Repeat if you're
a man. Tell me!

431
00:50:16,080 --> 00:50:24,060
If I don't pull your flesh from your bones
I shall not be called Konur, numbskull!

432
00:50:27,230 --> 00:50:29,760
Untie him!

433
00:50:47,750 --> 00:50:49,050
Mongol dog!

434
00:50:49,050 --> 00:50:50,670
Get him up!

435
00:51:05,780 --> 00:51:07,410
Don't!

436
00:51:29,420 --> 00:51:31,270
Infidel!

437
00:51:59,050 --> 00:52:02,160
Göktuğ. Göktuğ come here, son.

438
00:52:14,160 --> 00:52:17,180
Mother! Look I have the same one.

439
00:52:17,420 --> 00:52:21,420
Of course, you do, son. All of our
men have it since your grandfather.

440
00:52:44,070 --> 00:52:46,260
- Father!
- Father.

441
00:52:46,260 --> 00:52:49,080
- Konur! Göktuğ!
- My Bey...

442
00:52:50,990 --> 00:52:55,280
- Father!
- My Bey!

443
00:53:07,600 --> 00:53:09,640
Father!

444
00:53:23,330 --> 00:53:25,050
You degenerate!

445
00:53:32,100 --> 00:53:33,600
You dog!

446
00:53:36,180 --> 00:53:38,610
I'll teach you how to laugh.

447
00:53:39,960 --> 00:53:43,200
Don't rely on Osman Bey to save you.

448
00:53:43,350 --> 00:53:47,350
As long as we're here, this world
will be hell for you!

449
00:53:56,890 --> 00:53:58,380
Konur!

450
00:54:04,720 --> 00:54:09,110
Balgay's words. Until he says
something, they will live.

451
00:54:32,490 --> 00:54:34,160
Konur!

452
00:54:53,080 --> 00:54:54,370
Selamın Aleyküm
(Peace be upon you)

453
00:54:54,370 --> 00:54:56,590
Aleyküm Selam.
(Peace be upon you too)

454
00:54:58,420 --> 00:55:06,510
Since you're here safe and sound, you've
rekindled Balgay's desire for power.

455
00:55:11,240 --> 00:55:20,590
Now I will save my brothers, my Selcan
mother, my Tent from Balgay's wrath.

456
00:55:21,490 --> 00:55:26,480
Then, if Allah permits, our first
great battle will begin.

457
00:55:31,150 --> 00:55:35,150
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.
( in the name of Allah, the merciful and compassionate.)

458
00:55:37,110 --> 00:55:39,800
I took care of it well.

459
00:55:49,860 --> 00:55:52,540
May Allah bless you, my Sheikh.

460
00:55:54,350 --> 00:55:57,220
Your first battle with the Mongols.

461
00:55:58,120 --> 00:56:02,120
First battles are harsh.
They're very hard.

462
00:56:03,310 --> 00:56:09,080
When our Prophet, with his companion,
started his first battle of Badr...

463
00:56:09,080 --> 00:56:14,060
... non-muslims were underestimating
the holy army with their arrogance.

464
00:56:16,240 --> 00:56:18,780
They were bragging about their power.

465
00:56:19,030 --> 00:56:23,030
Because of that, they
underestimated Muslims.

466
00:56:24,200 --> 00:56:30,700
But our Prophet was always alert.

467
00:56:34,070 --> 00:56:42,920
Our Prophet went to the
battlefield of Badr before non-muslims...

468
00:56:43,700 --> 00:56:47,460
... and had the shafts closed one by one.

469
00:56:49,530 --> 00:56:55,050
He made moves to compensate for his
weakness in the hot weather of the desert.

470
00:56:57,000 --> 00:57:01,080
After completing his preparations...

471
00:57:01,090 --> 00:57:04,270
... he started praying.

472
00:57:07,120 --> 00:57:13,050
The Prophet of mercy trusted Allah
with his army.

473
00:57:17,120 --> 00:57:20,380
And my Allah answered his prayers.

474
00:57:21,920 --> 00:57:26,960
My Rab says, in the surah Ali İmran...

475
00:57:28,110 --> 00:57:38,440
While you were weaker in Badr,
Allah helped you and made you victorious.

476
00:57:44,100 --> 00:57:48,560
Live by Allah's words...

477
00:57:49,860 --> 00:57:51,890
... so that you'll be grateful.

478
00:58:02,470 --> 00:58:09,000
I hope my Allah supports us with army of
Angels so that we'll be victorious.

479
00:58:16,050 --> 00:58:18,430
It's up to you, Osman.

480
00:58:19,840 --> 00:58:21,760
What do you mean, my Sheikh?

481
00:58:23,260 --> 00:58:26,910
Don't lose your sincerity and faith.

482
00:58:27,360 --> 00:58:30,490
Do everything with passion.

483
00:58:31,820 --> 00:58:36,970
A job without passion
won't yield good results.

484
00:58:41,550 --> 00:58:47,900
But this passion shouldn't just be love.

485
00:58:52,120 --> 00:58:59,180
Our Prophet was stoned for
his love for Allah in Ta'if.

486
00:59:00,190 --> 00:59:03,190
He didn't bow to the cruel.

487
00:59:03,790 --> 00:59:07,010
The enemy couldn't scare him.

488
00:59:10,390 --> 00:59:15,000
You shouldn't lose your passion...

489
00:59:15,330 --> 00:59:20,180
... while setting your table,
swinging your sword...

490
00:59:20,490 --> 00:59:23,630
... while talking in a meeting, or
listening to someone's troubles.

491
00:59:24,670 --> 00:59:27,410
If you lose it...

492
00:59:28,260 --> 00:59:31,110
... you'll lose your consciousness.

493
00:59:32,300 --> 00:59:37,190
The devil will enslave you.

494
00:59:37,790 --> 00:59:41,160
Make your mind one with passion, my son.

495
00:59:42,390 --> 00:59:49,030
So that these dark clouds over
the world of Islam can go away.

496
00:59:50,560 --> 00:59:53,120
So that the hopelessness comes to an end.

497
00:59:53,120 --> 00:59:55,800
So that laziness comes to an end.

498
00:59:58,000 --> 01:00:01,870
So that the fire of resurrection
can be rekindled.

499
01:00:06,390 --> 01:00:08,410
Hopefully, my Sheikh.

500
01:00:09,540 --> 01:00:14,510
I'll try my best.
I'll fight until the end!

501
01:00:15,830 --> 01:00:23,240
Come on. Balgay will go mad
if we talk for too long.

502
01:00:30,170 --> 01:00:33,510
- Ya Allah!
- Ya Bismillah!

503
01:01:05,190 --> 01:01:06,650
Konur.

504
01:01:08,340 --> 01:01:10,160
What are you thinking, son?

505
01:01:13,050 --> 01:01:15,210
Nothing, mother.

506
01:01:15,380 --> 01:01:16,820
Tell me.

507
01:01:18,700 --> 01:01:23,100
I had a small mind. Kungar took it.

508
01:01:24,440 --> 01:01:26,360
What are you talking about, son?

509
01:01:27,380 --> 01:01:31,220
Please don't be him. Please don't be him.

510
01:01:31,940 --> 01:01:35,330
Please don't be him. Please don't be him.

511
01:01:37,160 --> 01:01:40,060
My Allah, please.

512
01:01:57,800 --> 01:02:00,120
What is it, Princess?

513
01:02:00,940 --> 01:02:04,940
Did you lose your way?
What are you doing in our Tent?

514
01:02:05,730 --> 01:02:08,530
I'm here to say "Get well soon".

515
01:02:08,530 --> 01:02:10,380
Come here.

516
01:02:15,470 --> 01:02:18,320
Did the Mongols hurt you much?

517
01:02:27,560 --> 01:02:30,880
Osman Bey probably worries about you.

518
01:02:36,800 --> 01:02:38,940
They ruined you.

519
01:02:40,280 --> 01:02:42,190
Look at them!

520
01:02:47,500 --> 01:02:49,400
My Allah, forgive me.

521
01:02:49,400 --> 01:02:56,540
We weren't Tentless for a thousand years,
and weren't obsolete for a thousand years.

522
01:02:58,500 --> 01:03:03,490
If we were to be scared of snakes
like you and Balgay...

523
01:03:03,490 --> 01:03:06,160
... we wouldn't be standing
in front of you right now.

524
01:03:06,310 --> 01:03:10,430
You're talking to me, tied
in your own dungeon.

525
01:03:14,270 --> 01:03:16,870
You're miserable.

526
01:03:22,050 --> 01:03:29,570
My Osman made Balgay kick
Alişar like the dog he is.

527
01:03:29,730 --> 01:03:37,180
Alişar is gone. Now is this Princess after
Balgay's mattress?

528
01:03:45,550 --> 01:03:48,470
What is it, Princess?

529
01:03:51,540 --> 01:03:55,300
My words hurt the Princess' arrogance.

530
01:03:57,260 --> 01:04:02,060
You're dying to take the life
Balgay couldn't.

531
01:04:04,210 --> 01:04:07,840
I'll only laugh to that, Sofia.

532
01:04:09,340 --> 01:04:12,430
When your Tent is covered in your blood...

533
01:04:14,810 --> 01:04:18,070
... the last thing you'll see will be
my laughing eyes.

534
01:04:21,980 --> 01:04:24,110
Selcan Hatun.

535
01:04:24,520 --> 01:04:30,430
We will not die without putting
those eyes of yours out!

536
01:04:30,430 --> 01:04:34,190
Without seeing you skinned alive...

537
01:04:34,900 --> 01:04:36,440
... I will not die.

538
01:04:45,190 --> 01:04:48,740
I will come to your funerals.

539
01:05:11,950 --> 01:05:14,240
Look at us.

540
01:05:17,720 --> 01:05:20,310
My dear Allah...

541
01:05:21,790 --> 01:05:23,960
No words from Osman Bey either.

542
01:05:25,180 --> 01:05:27,570
We don't know what he's doing.

543
01:05:33,570 --> 01:05:36,000
How are we going to put up with this?

544
01:05:39,130 --> 01:05:46,880
Kill us. Kills us! Kill us!
Kill us!

545
01:05:46,880 --> 01:05:48,370
Friends!

546
01:05:50,480 --> 01:05:52,120
Brothers!

547
01:05:53,670 --> 01:05:58,250
Allah says in the Quran...

548
01:05:59,980 --> 01:06:03,690
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.
( in the name of Allah, the merciful and compassionate.)

549
01:06:06,730 --> 01:06:11,720
Unless you go through which
those before you went through...

550
01:06:12,030 --> 01:06:14,430
... you cannot enter heaven.

551
01:06:15,640 --> 01:06:18,570
Having faith with words is easy.

552
01:06:19,280 --> 01:06:22,600
But having patience during
trials is hard, brothers.

553
01:06:25,110 --> 01:06:26,890
Brothers!

554
01:06:27,470 --> 01:06:31,500
Patience, brothers!
Patience.

555
01:06:33,000 --> 01:06:34,580
Patience.

556
01:06:40,360 --> 01:06:42,470
Patience, my Allah.

557
01:06:46,800 --> 01:06:49,360
How can this woman come to our Tent?

558
01:06:49,380 --> 01:06:51,420
I'll go take a look.

559
01:06:59,620 --> 01:07:05,460
Let me go! What is that
snake Sofia doing in my Tent?

560
01:07:05,460 --> 01:07:08,300
You won't leave your Tent before
Osman Bey comes!

561
01:07:21,450 --> 01:07:26,440
If she comes to the Tent after killing
countless valiants of ours...

562
01:07:26,440 --> 01:07:31,390
... they are working with Balgay.
They won't stop before killing us all.

563
01:07:32,320 --> 01:07:38,640
I should have killed that snake
the first time she came to the Tent.

564
01:07:40,590 --> 01:07:43,480
You never do things in time, Dündar Bey.

565
01:07:43,830 --> 01:07:47,260
You didn't listen to me when I told you
to look after Osman.

566
01:07:47,260 --> 01:07:51,370
"Stop Edebali" I said. You didn't listen.

567
01:07:51,370 --> 01:07:56,660
Now they have joined forces and they are
taking our Tent and our lives!

568
01:07:57,100 --> 01:07:59,000
Zöhre. Enough.

569
01:07:59,210 --> 01:08:04,170
They are going to take away our son.
They will break us.

570
01:08:04,180 --> 01:08:08,620
It's all because of Osman.
If they kill my son...

571
01:08:08,620 --> 01:08:11,630
I will haunt you in the afterworld!

572
01:08:11,630 --> 01:08:15,350
Hatun, I said enough.
Enough!

573
01:08:15,350 --> 01:08:19,680
You couldn't protect this tent.
You couldn't take care of Osman.

574
01:08:19,680 --> 01:08:22,600
- Are you taking it all out of me now?
- Enough!

575
01:08:22,600 --> 01:08:25,430
Come on, hit me!

576
01:08:25,810 --> 01:08:29,140
You can fear only me.

577
01:08:30,080 --> 01:08:33,300
Enough already.

578
01:08:42,220 --> 01:08:46,390
Enough, enough enough!

579
01:08:46,870 --> 01:08:51,850
Enough, enough enough!

580
01:08:52,140 --> 01:08:55,450
Enough, enough enough!

581
01:08:57,970 --> 01:08:59,540
Enough.

582
01:09:10,260 --> 01:09:13,540
You will crawl into Balgay's presence,
Hatun.

583
01:09:47,840 --> 01:09:50,390
What did you bring me?

584
01:09:53,060 --> 01:09:57,110
Efendi Yannis aroused the spies in
Byzantine.

585
01:10:00,580 --> 01:10:03,050
We are ready for the big war.

586
01:10:10,510 --> 01:10:13,190
As I said to Yannis...

587
01:10:14,100 --> 01:10:18,070
Every information coming from castles...

588
01:10:18,250 --> 01:10:22,730
from landlords, from Emperor's
armies...

589
01:10:23,450 --> 01:10:26,430
should be brought to me first.

590
01:10:30,660 --> 01:10:33,420
Don't doubt that.

591
01:10:38,790 --> 01:10:45,520
The landlord of Yakhisar will come to see
you. He will not die before he sees you.

592
01:10:48,610 --> 01:10:53,420
The rest is your Nökers'(soldier) job.

593
01:10:55,820 --> 01:10:57,380
Get up.

594
01:11:07,790 --> 01:11:10,590
What else will you give me?

595
01:11:12,590 --> 01:11:16,440
This doesn't work, me giving all the time,
Balgay.

596
01:11:20,620 --> 01:11:25,550
I want you to keep your promises.

597
01:11:31,940 --> 01:11:36,180
How dare you talk to me like that,
Princess?

598
01:11:38,440 --> 01:11:43,470
Why didn't you kill Osman and his Alps
when they came to you?

599
01:11:45,320 --> 01:11:48,600
How do you know that Osman is
in the tribe?

600
01:11:49,180 --> 01:11:52,510
I said I have eyes everywhere.

601
01:11:53,270 --> 01:11:56,060
Even in Turks' tent.

602
01:11:58,270 --> 01:12:00,720
Didn't you believe us?

603
01:12:03,390 --> 01:12:05,780
I freed Osman.

604
01:12:05,810 --> 01:12:08,230
Genghis Khan's laws.

605
01:12:10,380 --> 01:12:13,170
Why are they so important?

606
01:12:13,170 --> 01:12:15,430
So, you also know about this.

607
01:12:15,640 --> 01:12:20,340
And you believed Osman.

608
01:12:26,920 --> 01:12:28,540
Right?

609
01:12:31,010 --> 01:12:36,500
He will get what he wants when he
brings the laws.

610
01:12:38,830 --> 01:12:43,360
I swore on Genghis Khan's laws.

611
01:12:43,860 --> 01:12:46,110
Let's say he brought them.

612
01:12:47,980 --> 01:12:49,860
Then what?

613
01:12:50,850 --> 01:12:53,340
Once I get what I want to get...

614
01:12:55,410 --> 01:13:00,200
Then you can face with Osman.

615
01:13:41,700 --> 01:13:44,500
Osman Bey is coming, Commander
Balgay.

616
01:13:45,700 --> 01:13:47,830
Let's see.

617
01:14:17,600 --> 01:14:20,850
Genghis Khan's laws, ha?

618
01:14:21,530 --> 01:14:28,120
Are you dreaming of being an Empress of
Constantinopolis with your new owner, Sofia?

619
01:14:30,260 --> 01:14:33,100
My eyes are sharper than yours.

620
01:14:33,140 --> 01:14:35,110
My ears are better than yours.

621
01:14:35,170 --> 01:14:37,690
My weapon is sharper than yours.

622
01:14:37,830 --> 01:14:42,700
Osman, you are trying to
bite off more than you can chew.

623
01:14:44,080 --> 01:14:50,300
If you are desiring death so much, don't
tire us.

624
01:14:51,020 --> 01:14:54,100
I will face you someday, Sofia.

625
01:14:54,220 --> 01:14:57,140
And that day is soon.

626
01:14:58,330 --> 01:15:01,830
Did you bring Genghis Khan's laws?

627
01:15:03,200 --> 01:15:04,500
Hmh?

628
01:15:04,720 --> 01:15:11,320
I want to see, but I have lots of things
to do in the castle.

629
01:15:14,170 --> 01:15:16,990
Say hi to Yannis.

630
01:15:19,290 --> 01:15:21,430
I will see you again.

631
01:15:21,820 --> 01:15:24,970
Say hi to Edebalı.

632
01:15:25,540 --> 01:15:30,940
"Sofia will kill you soon."

633
01:15:49,500 --> 01:15:51,270
Did you bring it?

634
01:15:52,180 --> 01:15:54,010
Yes.

635
01:16:04,470 --> 01:16:06,250
Bring it to me.

636
01:16:10,630 --> 01:16:13,810
Don't forget the word you gave in front
of Beys.

637
01:16:28,400 --> 01:16:32,790
Keep your promise.
Get out of my father's place.

638
01:16:39,390 --> 01:16:41,250
Enough.

639
01:16:49,550 --> 01:16:52,790
Give me the law.

640
01:17:52,640 --> 01:17:54,720
Keep your promise.

641
01:17:55,180 --> 01:17:57,230
Release my alps.

642
01:17:58,010 --> 01:18:00,670
Get your Nökers(soldiers) out of
my tent.

643
01:18:03,260 --> 01:18:05,920
Power...

644
01:18:08,470 --> 01:18:10,840
is with me.

645
01:18:15,930 --> 01:18:20,490
If you don't keep your promise, Geyhatu'll
figure out that you have Genghis Khan's laws.

646
01:18:20,550 --> 01:18:23,840
An alp of mine is waiting to notify
Geyhatu.

647
01:18:26,900 --> 01:18:31,950
Do you know why I offered you to
be banner lord?

648
01:18:33,090 --> 01:18:37,190
In time, Genghis Khan's biggest enemies...

649
01:18:37,220 --> 01:18:41,120
had been his best friends...

650
01:18:41,120 --> 01:18:45,500
his best Commanders.

651
01:18:54,880 --> 01:19:00,060
In a fight, a valiant shot an arrow
to Genghis Khan.

652
01:19:01,110 --> 01:19:03,920
And succeeded to injure him.

653
01:19:04,400 --> 01:19:10,290
After the war was over, his Commander
Tayhatlu went to the captivities.

654
01:19:10,830 --> 01:19:13,360
He asked who shot that arrow.

655
01:19:13,740 --> 01:19:20,410
A soldier came to the front with
courage and said " I shot it."

656
01:19:20,790 --> 01:19:27,100
Genghis Khan was impressed by his courage
and made him the Commander of his army...

657
01:19:27,500 --> 01:19:34,010
and also gave him Cebe name, which means
arrow.

658
01:19:34,760 --> 01:19:41,860
Cebe has been one of the greatest
Commanders of Mongol Army.

659
01:19:43,770 --> 01:19:49,420
Firstly, I am Allah's creature, then
Ertuğrul Ghazi's son.

660
01:19:51,110 --> 01:19:55,520
We obey Allah, and then our tradition.

661
01:19:57,770 --> 01:20:02,960
Now, get out of the tent with
your soldiers.

662
01:20:16,540 --> 01:20:18,600
Can I come in, Bamsı Bey?

663
01:20:18,780 --> 01:20:20,800
Come, Nuğrul.

664
01:20:23,660 --> 01:20:26,670
- Osman Bey has come.
- So, it is time.

665
01:20:27,350 --> 01:20:30,580
We can't trust that Balgay dog.

666
01:20:30,590 --> 01:20:36,490
Lions, you heard me. I will slaughter them
if they don't keep their promise.

667
01:20:36,590 --> 01:20:39,350
- Is the carriage ready?
- Everything is ready, my Bey.

668
01:20:39,350 --> 01:20:44,180
- You trained us for this day, for sure.
- Masha Allah(praise be) my valiant.

669
01:20:44,810 --> 01:20:50,380
Mongol infidels will see what it takes
to conquer Muslim lands.

670
01:20:50,510 --> 01:20:55,360
You have gazelle eyes, but you have
a wolf's heart. Masha Allah my daughter.

671
01:21:14,170 --> 01:21:16,810
Osman brought Genghis Khan's laws.

672
01:21:17,680 --> 01:21:20,900
No one can stop Balgay now.

673
01:21:21,760 --> 01:21:23,880
Samsa Bey.

674
01:21:27,790 --> 01:21:30,570
How did Osman find that?

675
01:21:33,930 --> 01:21:36,720
I don't know how he got it but...

676
01:21:38,840 --> 01:21:43,590
Osman Bey will gather all the Mongols
while trying to save us.

677
01:21:44,340 --> 01:21:45,810
Samsa Bey...

678
01:21:46,340 --> 01:21:49,250
Osman Bey must know something.

679
01:21:50,360 --> 01:21:57,530
Sure. There are so many things that
he knows but we don't, brother.

680
01:22:06,820 --> 01:22:13,550
Today, the souls gave you hope, and
they gave me power.

681
01:22:16,080 --> 01:22:19,550
Cerkutay, set the captives free.

682
01:22:20,240 --> 01:22:25,030
They should know that Balgay
has spared their lives.

683
01:22:34,840 --> 01:22:36,500
Dündar Bey.

684
01:22:39,500 --> 01:22:42,730
Notify the near Beys immediately.

685
01:22:43,320 --> 01:22:47,730
Say that "Go to Balgay's presence."

686
01:22:48,250 --> 01:22:54,650
"Balgay wants to see if there's someone who
is thirsty for his blood.

687
01:22:55,090 --> 01:22:58,800
who looks for trouble...

688
01:22:58,800 --> 01:23:04,790
who rides for a fall."

689
01:23:06,680 --> 01:23:12,820
Tell them to come to me to obey me.

690
01:23:37,220 --> 01:23:42,920
How did you get Cengiz Han's laws, eh?

691
01:23:43,060 --> 01:23:46,860
Why don't I know about that, Osman?

692
01:23:47,110 --> 01:23:48,900
Uncle...

693
01:23:48,920 --> 01:23:53,460
I saved valiants' lives and protected the
tribe.

694
01:23:54,470 --> 01:24:00,260
Now, you need to think about how
you will manage my father's place.

695
01:24:02,680 --> 01:24:07,940
From now on, I don't want any rebellion.

696
01:24:08,510 --> 01:24:11,020
Watch your steps.

697
01:24:11,070 --> 01:24:14,460
My Batur was going to die because of you.

698
01:24:14,460 --> 01:24:18,750
You were almost going to poison my son
like you did to your Alps.

699
01:24:18,750 --> 01:24:21,470
This is the poison of freedom, Uncle.

700
01:24:21,840 --> 01:24:26,590
When it mixes with the blood, it doesn't
go away, if you are a real man.

701
01:24:26,590 --> 01:24:32,290
They will destroy the Tent because of
your stubbornness!

702
01:24:32,550 --> 01:24:35,630
Enough already.

703
01:24:35,640 --> 01:24:42,090
They destroy the Tent or you obey
Balgay like a dog. Doesn't matter.

704
01:24:42,340 --> 01:24:46,340
Get out of that place so that someone
qualified can run this tribe!

705
01:24:47,350 --> 01:24:52,880
Who will take my place when I quit?

706
01:24:53,060 --> 01:24:55,730
- Who!?
- I will!

707
01:24:58,220 --> 01:25:01,680
Ertuğrul Ghazi's son Osman!

708
01:25:07,660 --> 01:25:09,920
There's a meeting tonight.

709
01:25:10,810 --> 01:25:13,690
You'll answer, Osman.

710
01:25:13,880 --> 01:25:15,750
You'll answer.

711
01:25:22,450 --> 01:25:28,190
We can't trust them. Observe both Kayı
Tent and Samsa's Tent.

712
01:25:28,270 --> 01:25:30,460
As you command, Balgay.

713
01:25:36,000 --> 01:25:37,710
Get out of here!

714
01:25:43,400 --> 01:25:47,020
Osman found a way to save his tribe.

715
01:25:47,110 --> 01:25:49,280
How did he manage that?

716
01:25:49,300 --> 01:25:52,960
- How did he get Genghis Khan laws?
- Sir...

717
01:25:52,960 --> 01:25:56,510
Perhaps this is Edebalı and Ahis' job.

718
01:25:56,510 --> 01:25:59,540
Damn Edebalı and Ahis.

719
01:25:59,540 --> 01:26:04,370
Not Edebalı. Even he can't do this.

720
01:26:05,880 --> 01:26:09,390
There must be something else.
But what is that?

721
01:26:09,390 --> 01:26:14,240
- Salvador, didn't Osman say anything?
- No sir.

722
01:26:14,240 --> 01:26:18,360
Whatever this secret is, Osman hides
it to death.

723
01:26:18,360 --> 01:26:22,940
Then he will not be able to hide it
so long.

724
01:26:23,940 --> 01:26:26,760
As soon as Balgay gives up on him...

725
01:26:28,780 --> 01:26:31,700
I will hunt Osman down.

726
01:26:33,270 --> 01:26:36,960
We have a hound who shows us the way.

727
01:26:38,760 --> 01:26:43,280
He knows our prey very well.

728
01:26:43,900 --> 01:26:48,340
Moreover, everything he said until now
has been proved true.

729
01:26:49,930 --> 01:26:54,260
I told you I wouldn't die before
redeeming myself, sir Yannis.

730
01:26:54,390 --> 01:26:57,430
I know where he hides Edebalı.

731
01:26:57,960 --> 01:27:01,150
We will hunt them all at once.

732
01:27:24,970 --> 01:27:26,580
Osman.

733
01:27:26,810 --> 01:27:29,320
Thank Allah you are okay.

734
01:27:31,180 --> 01:27:33,490
Thank Allah.

735
01:27:34,560 --> 01:27:37,290
Salvation is soon, Bala Hatun.

736
01:27:37,490 --> 01:27:40,900
We will repel Mongols, inshallah.

737
01:27:42,960 --> 01:27:45,530
How did you manage that, Osman Bey?

738
01:27:46,160 --> 01:27:50,410
Genghis Khan's laws have been absent
for years.

739
01:27:50,960 --> 01:27:52,900
How did you find it?

740
01:27:53,290 --> 01:27:57,800
There is a saying " The helper doesn't
show up when you are not in need."

741
01:27:59,190 --> 01:28:02,310
Let's say the helper has arrived.

742
01:28:02,980 --> 01:28:05,530
Who is that helper, Osman Bey?

743
01:28:13,420 --> 01:28:15,700
It's secret, Bala Hatun.

744
01:28:16,670 --> 01:28:19,190
Won't you tell me, Osman Bey?

745
01:28:20,110 --> 01:28:26,390
Won't you tell the woman who you love,
who you would set the whole world on fire?

746
01:28:27,130 --> 01:28:29,390
Now, know that...

747
01:28:30,210 --> 01:28:33,190
if you want to share a life with me...

748
01:28:34,420 --> 01:28:37,290
you are not going to know my secrets.

749
01:28:38,230 --> 01:28:41,110
You will stop when I say so.

750
01:28:42,280 --> 01:28:47,830
You will keep silent when silence
is needed.

751
01:28:50,770 --> 01:28:53,340
I am an Ahi daughter, Osman Bey.

752
01:28:54,630 --> 01:28:59,230
If I am going to be a friend to my husband,
I want to know his secrets.

753
01:29:00,020 --> 01:29:03,250
I want to stand like a mountain
on his side.

754
01:29:03,570 --> 01:29:07,400
I want to fight together.

755
01:29:07,610 --> 01:29:11,320
I am not like other Hatuns.

756
01:29:16,510 --> 01:29:18,530
If you allow...

757
01:29:19,650 --> 01:29:21,640
It's all yours.

758
01:29:35,050 --> 01:29:36,720
Salamu alaykum.

759
01:29:36,720 --> 01:29:40,430
- Salamu alaykum.
- Alaykum salam.

760
01:29:55,780 --> 01:29:57,940
You did it.

761
01:29:58,540 --> 01:30:01,440
You saved us, my Bey.

762
01:30:07,290 --> 01:30:09,490
What is it, Sergeant Samsa?

763
01:30:10,920 --> 01:30:13,110
You are staying away.

764
01:30:15,470 --> 01:30:17,690
How did this happen, Osman Bey?

765
01:30:18,850 --> 01:30:22,780
How did that infidel release us?

766
01:30:26,060 --> 01:30:29,320
There's always a key for every lock,
Samsa Bey.

767
01:30:29,940 --> 01:30:34,440
The important thing is who owns the key.

768
01:30:34,440 --> 01:30:36,230
You are wrong, Samsa Bey.

769
01:30:36,530 --> 01:30:40,100
The important thing is whether the
key works or not.

770
01:30:40,180 --> 01:30:43,840
That key worked, so we are free now.

771
01:30:44,570 --> 01:30:47,340
What is friendship, Osman Bey?

772
01:30:48,120 --> 01:30:50,090
What is brotherhood?

773
01:30:50,630 --> 01:30:53,070
Why don't you tell us?

774
01:30:53,300 --> 01:30:56,630
No one gave us our freedom, Samsa Bey.

775
01:30:56,830 --> 01:30:58,520
We took it.

776
01:31:04,110 --> 01:31:06,840
I can't tell this to anyone.

777
01:31:08,970 --> 01:31:14,070
I thought we were like a chain of mountains
when we stood back to back.

778
01:31:14,410 --> 01:31:16,420
But I was wrong.

779
01:31:17,120 --> 01:31:25,450
I, the great Samsa Bey, ignored my
personality and served you like an Alp.

780
01:31:25,450 --> 01:31:30,720
Samsa Bey, we are facing the cruels.

781
01:31:31,130 --> 01:31:33,830
We are going through difficult times.

782
01:31:33,830 --> 01:31:38,360
- If we don't tolerate each other...
- Apparently, we are not close now.

783
01:31:38,770 --> 01:31:42,870
Apparently, for you,
the wind blows in reverse.

784
01:31:43,690 --> 01:31:49,100
When I feel that I am not trusted...

785
01:31:49,510 --> 01:31:52,060
I no longer continue that way.

786
01:31:53,260 --> 01:31:57,350
- Samsa Bey.
- So, this is it.

787
01:31:58,680 --> 01:32:03,990
Now that a secret is between us, I can
walk the freedom way alone.

788
01:32:10,680 --> 01:32:14,390
I give my blessings to you.

789
01:33:25,940 --> 01:33:46,790
Happiness is Genghis Khan's
Law is Balgay's.

790
01:35:28,190 --> 01:35:34,800
Genghis Khan's soul is in me.

791
01:35:40,960 --> 01:35:45,470
His law is with me!

792
01:36:14,700 --> 01:36:17,350
From now on...

793
01:36:18,990 --> 01:36:22,690
From now on, with Genghis Khan's soul...

794
01:36:22,740 --> 01:36:26,450
with his power...

795
01:36:26,950 --> 01:36:33,270
To north, to south, to east, to west...

796
01:36:33,310 --> 01:36:40,470
to lands, to seas, to mountains, and
to sky...

797
01:36:40,490 --> 01:36:44,870
I am the ruler!

798
01:36:45,070 --> 01:36:48,590
The souls are with me.

799
01:36:48,980 --> 01:36:56,700
My anger is in me.
My blood is boiling

800
01:37:10,690 --> 01:37:17,300
Here, in front of you,
my valiant soldiers...

801
01:37:17,940 --> 01:37:21,950
my loyal Nökers...

802
01:37:22,110 --> 01:37:26,440
in front of my deceased
ancestors' souls...

803
01:37:26,870 --> 01:37:31,960
and in front of the soul of almighty
Genghis Khan.

804
01:37:45,920 --> 01:37:53,080
I will seal Genghis Khan's law
in my tongue!

805
01:38:01,720 --> 01:38:08,010
This is Balgay's swear in front of...

806
01:38:08,010 --> 01:38:11,640
my Nökers whose friends are our
ancestors' souls.

807
01:38:16,880 --> 01:38:20,820
We set off to rule the whole world.

808
01:38:20,960 --> 01:38:28,120
We went beyond Gobi Desert,
Tengri Mountains, and the Caspian Sea.

809
01:38:28,240 --> 01:38:32,020
Our destination is Constantinople.

810
01:38:32,080 --> 01:38:35,720
Our way is bloody!

811
01:38:35,720 --> 01:38:37,910
Blood!

812
01:38:51,780 --> 01:38:57,490
Neither Byzantine's dogs nor peevish
Turks...

813
01:38:57,710 --> 01:39:02,090
can stop us.

814
01:39:03,640 --> 01:39:08,320
Rebels like Osman...

815
01:39:09,860 --> 01:39:15,230
will be material for our shaman drums.

816
01:39:15,430 --> 01:39:24,160
We will rise upon their bodies by banging
their skins with their bones!

817
01:39:24,160 --> 01:39:28,820
We will swim in their blood!

818
01:39:36,290 --> 01:39:39,100
Crush me if I stop.

819
01:39:39,530 --> 01:39:45,050
Trample me under your horses
if I get exhausted.

820
01:39:50,180 --> 01:39:55,380
You shall be my enemy if you stop!

821
01:39:55,440 --> 01:39:59,820
If you stop, you shall suffer forever...

822
01:40:00,130 --> 01:40:05,930
in the souls hands!

823
01:40:29,930 --> 01:40:35,490
I am sealing Genghis Khan's law
in my tongue.

824
01:40:35,830 --> 01:40:39,860
Happiness is Genghis Khan's
Law is Balgay's.

825
01:41:33,830 --> 01:41:37,150
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.
[in the name of Allah, the merciful and compassionate.]

826
01:41:37,150 --> 01:41:39,430
With Allah's ninety nine names...

827
01:41:39,640 --> 01:41:46,670
who can make things happen with
a single voice.

828
01:41:59,170 --> 01:42:04,160
My Beys, we are going through difficult
days.

829
01:42:04,280 --> 01:42:11,620
Mongols said they went away, but they
may come back anytime.

830
01:42:13,600 --> 01:42:17,980
We are here to review our situation.

831
01:42:18,790 --> 01:42:20,920
I've been in Kayı tent for years.

832
01:42:20,920 --> 01:42:24,790
I've never heard of anyone
doing something without Bey's knowledge.

833
01:42:25,070 --> 01:42:31,830
Osman, without the council's and your
knowledge, did things about Mongols...

834
01:42:31,830 --> 01:42:33,920
Dündar Bey.

835
01:42:36,810 --> 01:42:41,560
We have heard that you declined Balgay's
offer of being a banner lord.

836
01:42:42,320 --> 01:42:45,310
How can you do that?

837
01:42:46,300 --> 01:42:51,680
If Osman had accepted this great offer
in the view of politics...

838
01:42:51,710 --> 01:42:53,580
those things wouldn't happen now.

839
01:42:53,600 --> 01:42:55,880
Wouldn't happen for now.

840
01:42:57,170 --> 01:42:59,350
What about the future?

841
01:42:59,710 --> 01:43:01,360
Our descendants will think that...

842
01:43:01,390 --> 01:43:04,580
we've been enslaved by Mongols.

843
01:43:05,350 --> 01:43:09,620
They'll think we've run away and
we've not struggled for freedom.

844
01:43:16,120 --> 01:43:18,000
I ask you.

845
01:43:18,330 --> 01:43:21,320
In this world, which we couldn't rule...

846
01:43:22,330 --> 01:43:26,330
will we bow down to Mongols?

847
01:43:26,890 --> 01:43:28,330
Will we receive orders?

848
01:43:28,550 --> 01:43:30,580
Will we be slaves?

849
01:43:31,270 --> 01:43:33,910
You don't talk right, my nephew.

850
01:43:34,060 --> 01:43:36,350
You're after some dreams.

851
01:43:36,630 --> 01:43:39,970
Will you defeat Mongols, who
rule the world?

852
01:43:40,030 --> 01:43:41,350
I will.

853
01:43:45,040 --> 01:43:47,040
You will.

854
01:43:47,530 --> 01:43:49,140
Dündar Bey will.

855
01:43:51,360 --> 01:43:53,140
Gündüz Bey will.

856
01:43:53,550 --> 01:43:55,120
Our blacksmith will.

857
01:43:56,580 --> 01:43:58,420
Şahin Bey will.

858
01:44:02,150 --> 01:44:05,880
We can defeat cruels...

859
01:44:06,650 --> 01:44:11,440
like how my father Kürşat have burnt
the great wall of China...

860
01:44:12,600 --> 01:44:16,600
like how my father Alparslan have brought
Romanos Diogenes to his knees...

861
01:44:17,970 --> 01:44:20,740
like how my father Selahattin have taken
Jerusalem.

862
01:44:22,590 --> 01:44:25,040
We should believe in ourselves.

863
01:44:26,570 --> 01:44:29,140
We don't want to hear nonsense, Osman.

864
01:44:29,160 --> 01:44:31,660
We don't want chaos anymore.

865
01:44:36,440 --> 01:44:38,680
This is a tent, Şahin Bey.

866
01:44:39,180 --> 01:44:43,490
There's a price for living in this land.
If someone doesn't pay for it...

867
01:44:43,760 --> 01:44:45,590
is destined to disappear.

868
01:44:45,590 --> 01:44:49,130
We're here because we've
paid for it, Gündüz Bey.

869
01:44:49,140 --> 01:44:51,150
We want silence now.

870
01:44:51,430 --> 01:44:55,430
- We want to rest.
- The ones who want to rest...

871
01:44:55,890 --> 01:44:58,770
shouldn't be in this tent.

872
01:44:58,880 --> 01:45:02,880
The ones who shouldn't
be in this tent are...

873
01:45:03,040 --> 01:45:06,270
the ones who get into trouble.

874
01:45:19,530 --> 01:45:24,160
What do you mean, blacksmith?

875
01:45:25,360 --> 01:45:27,620
Mongols are closer now.

876
01:45:28,380 --> 01:45:31,650
If we rebel, they'll kill us.

877
01:45:35,190 --> 01:45:38,890
We supported Osman because...

878
01:45:41,920 --> 01:45:43,870
he was the son of Ertuğrul Ghazi.

879
01:45:47,180 --> 01:45:50,090
But it's not bearable anymore.

880
01:45:53,580 --> 01:45:55,140
Osman...

881
01:46:01,600 --> 01:46:03,930
Osman should leave the tent.

882
01:47:05,090 --> 01:47:07,530
I thought you'd be happy.

883
01:47:07,530 --> 01:47:10,620
But you're angry.

884
01:47:10,870 --> 01:47:14,420
Osman Bey wants a slave, not a wife.

885
01:47:22,740 --> 01:47:24,290
What are you saying, Bala?

886
01:47:24,800 --> 01:47:27,770
He wants a wife like the women who
milk cows in his tent.

887
01:47:29,690 --> 01:47:33,530
I don't underrate them.

888
01:47:34,730 --> 01:47:37,410
I am sorry because
he doesn't know me well.

889
01:47:39,200 --> 01:47:42,120
He doesn't what kind of Hatun I am.

890
01:47:42,660 --> 01:47:43,660
Bala.

891
01:47:44,760 --> 01:47:48,950
If he doesn't, you know who you love.

892
01:47:51,440 --> 01:47:52,700
And the real skill is...

893
01:47:52,700 --> 01:47:57,070
how to tame the mad horses.

894
01:48:13,110 --> 01:48:14,900
Ah, Osman.

895
01:48:15,840 --> 01:48:16,910
Ah.

896
01:48:19,750 --> 01:48:23,880
- It's Osman's moves that save us.
- You're wrong, Gündüz Bey.

897
01:48:24,250 --> 01:48:28,640
It's Osman's moves that
have brought the Mongols here.

898
01:48:31,940 --> 01:48:35,160
You don't see the things in front of you.

899
01:48:37,150 --> 01:48:39,100
Sofia came here.

900
01:48:40,500 --> 01:48:44,170
The bad people are together and they
are alliances.

901
01:48:45,410 --> 01:48:47,360
Your only wish is to stay alive.

902
01:48:50,100 --> 01:48:52,170
What about your honor?

903
01:48:53,140 --> 01:48:58,170
When you followed my father, didn't you
know that these would happen to you?

904
01:48:59,050 --> 01:49:00,680
Tell me.

905
01:49:02,330 --> 01:49:03,670
Uncle.

906
01:49:04,610 --> 01:49:05,620
What about you?

907
01:49:08,890 --> 01:49:13,070
I came to these lands
having fought in many wars.

908
01:49:15,250 --> 01:49:19,250
We decided everything together...

909
01:49:19,950 --> 01:49:23,950
with your father, my brother
Ertuğrul Ghazi.

910
01:49:27,240 --> 01:49:31,470
No one in this tent can be a
callow as much as you.

911
01:49:45,250 --> 01:49:48,460
I told you many times, but...

912
01:49:49,060 --> 01:49:50,800
you didn't listen.

913
01:49:54,350 --> 01:49:58,350
The tent was routed. Söğüt is
about to fall.

914
01:49:59,000 --> 01:50:03,000
No one can resist a second strike.

915
01:50:09,960 --> 01:50:11,780
What about you, Bamsı Bey?

916
01:50:15,550 --> 01:50:17,440
You don't say anything.

917
01:50:18,410 --> 01:50:19,810
What do you say?

918
01:50:31,440 --> 01:50:33,180
Blacksmith...

919
01:50:33,410 --> 01:50:35,950
and Şahin Bey...

920
01:50:42,430 --> 01:50:44,050
are right.

921
01:51:03,130 --> 01:51:05,440
The tent needs to be...

922
01:51:05,730 --> 01:51:08,420
in peace, as soon as possible.

923
01:51:14,480 --> 01:51:16,160
Dündar Bey...

924
01:51:17,280 --> 01:51:19,540
the decision is yours.

925
01:51:24,460 --> 01:51:27,640
What about you, Abdurrahman Ghazi?

926
01:51:29,350 --> 01:51:32,840
You dedicated your life to Kayı's fight.

927
01:51:32,950 --> 01:51:35,620
You were the adjutant of Ertuğrul Ghazi.

928
01:51:35,710 --> 01:51:37,700
What do you say?

929
01:51:55,880 --> 01:51:58,430
Oghuzs' condition are apparent.

930
01:52:02,680 --> 01:52:04,930
The safety of the tent...

931
01:52:06,810 --> 01:52:09,100
is the most important.

932
01:52:14,360 --> 01:52:17,490
Bamsı Bey is right.

933
01:52:24,960 --> 01:52:28,960
I agree.

934
01:52:35,630 --> 01:52:38,230
For the safety of my tent...

935
01:52:40,470 --> 01:52:44,470
I approve the
exile of Osman.

936
01:52:53,900 --> 01:52:56,740
Your heart is frustrated.

937
01:52:56,750 --> 01:53:00,310
Do you object my words?

938
01:53:00,370 --> 01:53:04,540
If you talk again, I'll
send you to exile too.

939
01:53:06,640 --> 01:53:09,830
I'd rather die with Osman...

940
01:53:09,890 --> 01:53:12,520
than being captured here.

941
01:53:25,110 --> 01:53:29,110
So that my absence will
bring peace to the tent...

942
01:53:34,270 --> 01:53:36,730
then I'll go.

943
01:53:42,900 --> 01:53:44,470
But don't forget.

944
01:53:45,920 --> 01:53:49,920
Freedom is gained with weapons...

945
01:53:50,370 --> 01:53:52,290
not with peace and...

946
01:53:53,090 --> 01:53:55,610
facility.

947
01:54:53,450 --> 01:54:58,340
"Assalamu alaikum wa rahmatullah"
(peace and the mercy of Allah be on you)

948
01:55:18,630 --> 01:55:20,710
I have the same.

949
01:55:32,140 --> 01:55:34,000
My Allah...

950
01:55:34,170 --> 01:55:37,760
you've been testing Konur for years.

951
01:55:38,730 --> 01:55:42,730
I'm tired of longings.

952
01:55:44,310 --> 01:55:46,500
You see the best of me...

953
01:55:46,910 --> 01:55:48,760
and you know me well.

954
01:55:55,930 --> 01:55:57,050
If...

955
01:55:57,980 --> 01:56:01,510
the person who serves the Mongols...

956
01:56:02,810 --> 01:56:05,250
is my brother Göktuğ...

957
01:56:06,150 --> 01:56:08,570
you help him search for the right way.

958
01:56:10,200 --> 01:56:13,010
If he doesn't have faith...

959
01:56:15,340 --> 01:56:20,310
let me kill him with my own hands.

960
01:57:07,230 --> 01:57:08,660
Exile.

961
01:57:09,240 --> 01:57:13,240
- What are you saying, my Boran?
- Were going into exile tomorrow.

962
01:57:17,750 --> 01:57:22,210
Bamsı Bey? How did he let this?

963
01:57:23,210 --> 01:57:26,890
He and Abdurrahman Ghazi
wanted us to go, brother.

964
01:57:38,020 --> 01:57:41,820
Osman Bey said
we'd arrive Samsa Bey's tent.

965
01:57:42,720 --> 01:57:46,720
Sergeant Samsa? What if he
doesn't want us?

966
01:57:50,730 --> 01:57:53,480
I don't know, brother.

967
01:57:53,970 --> 01:57:57,520
My Boran. It's too bad.

968
01:58:21,360 --> 01:58:23,740
Can I come in, Bamsı Bey?

969
01:58:27,200 --> 01:58:29,450
Come in, Selcan Hatun.

970
01:58:37,500 --> 01:58:40,390
Bamsı Bey...

971
01:58:42,340 --> 01:58:44,950
That's unexpected.

972
01:58:45,860 --> 01:58:51,280
You're the half father
of Osman, you're his mentor...

973
01:58:52,980 --> 01:58:55,740
and you're his enemy now.

974
01:59:03,880 --> 01:59:07,410
I'm telling you, Bamsı Bey.

975
01:59:07,850 --> 01:59:10,490
Why do you turn away from him?

976
01:59:10,490 --> 01:59:13,780
Why do you leave him?

977
01:59:13,780 --> 01:59:17,420
Selcan Hatun, stop.

978
01:59:23,470 --> 01:59:27,470
Mongol fire burnt our tent.

979
01:59:31,580 --> 01:59:33,770
You saw it too.

980
01:59:34,850 --> 01:59:38,980
Mongols are like storms.

981
01:59:40,600 --> 01:59:43,710
- Bamsı Bey.
- Selcan Hatun.

982
01:59:44,790 --> 01:59:49,510
Beys are angry with him. He does
everything without asking.

983
01:59:53,880 --> 01:59:56,430
Osman should leave.

984
01:59:56,470 --> 02:00:00,470
So that he can pull himself together and
he can't be a novice.

985
02:00:07,270 --> 02:00:11,540
Selcan Hatun, you know.

986
02:00:12,470 --> 02:00:17,330
If Osman remains the
same, the tent will be miserable.

987
02:00:24,230 --> 02:00:27,300
Selcan Hatun, don't worry.

988
02:00:29,070 --> 02:00:32,620
I'll protect my Osman.

989
02:00:37,710 --> 02:00:40,140
Forgive me, Bamsı Bey.

990
02:00:40,770 --> 02:00:42,820
I have the heart of a mother.

991
02:00:43,040 --> 02:00:45,620
That's why I'm anxious.

992
02:00:48,350 --> 02:00:52,350
- Give me your blessings.
- Selcan Hatun.

993
02:00:52,490 --> 02:00:55,260
I know. Thanks.

994
02:01:20,780 --> 02:01:25,120
-Tashahhud Surah-

995
02:01:33,820 --> 02:01:40,500
"Assalamu alaikum wa rahmatullah" (peace and the mercy of Allah be on you)

996
02:01:46,260 --> 02:01:48,110
My Allah...

997
02:01:49,790 --> 02:01:52,980
If I'm struggling for myself...

998
02:01:54,390 --> 02:01:57,580
pull me together.

999
02:01:57,960 --> 02:02:02,100
If I'm struggling for reputation...

1000
02:02:03,560 --> 02:02:06,090
destroy me.

1001
02:02:08,580 --> 02:02:11,870
My only desire...

1002
02:02:13,040 --> 02:02:16,020
is to gain your consent.

1003
02:02:16,520 --> 02:02:20,090
If my desire...

1004
02:02:20,320 --> 02:02:22,510
becomes
reputation...

1005
02:02:24,150 --> 02:02:26,220
kill me.

1006
02:03:06,510 --> 02:03:08,130
I'm leaving, father.

1007
02:03:08,930 --> 02:03:09,970
I'm leaving.

1008
02:03:15,950 --> 02:03:17,890
But I'm proud.

1009
02:03:21,380 --> 02:03:24,410
I did everything for this tent.

1010
02:03:24,870 --> 02:03:28,520
I didn't bow down to the landlord.

1011
02:03:29,380 --> 02:03:31,860
I didn't bow down to the Mongols.

1012
02:03:39,890 --> 02:03:42,700
I learnt how to hold my head high
from you.

1013
02:03:46,950 --> 02:03:49,490
I learnt courage fom Bamsı Bey.

1014
02:03:51,420 --> 02:03:54,260
I learnt loyalty from Abdurrahman Ghazi.

1015
02:04:01,160 --> 02:04:03,330
Now I'm leaving.

1016
02:04:05,620 --> 02:04:08,050
But I'll come back.

1017
02:04:29,820 --> 02:04:30,940
Son.

1018
02:04:31,550 --> 02:04:34,130
You're the right owner of this tent.

1019
02:04:34,440 --> 02:04:39,690
- Dündar Bey sent you.
- No one can send me from this tent.

1020
02:04:41,650 --> 02:04:43,890
I won't go into exile.

1021
02:04:44,610 --> 02:04:48,610
If I stay, I'll have to depend on
Dündar Bey.

1022
02:04:50,830 --> 02:04:52,950
You know, I can't.

1023
02:04:56,890 --> 02:05:00,290
Come back soon. You know...

1024
02:05:00,530 --> 02:05:04,180
Dündar Bey isn't the one who'll
glorify the Kayıs.

1025
02:05:04,360 --> 02:05:07,890
What would we do without you?

1026
02:05:07,910 --> 02:05:09,950
Don't worry.

1027
02:05:10,330 --> 02:05:14,400
I won't leave this tent...

1028
02:05:14,400 --> 02:05:17,860
which my grandfather Süleyman Şah
and my father Ertuğrul Ghazi ruled.

1029
02:05:19,920 --> 02:05:24,600
If I don't go now, it'll be hard for
me to obey Dündar Bey.

1030
02:05:24,920 --> 02:05:27,090
It will.

1031
02:05:28,660 --> 02:05:30,390
If I go...

1032
02:05:31,040 --> 02:05:36,670
when the tiime comes, I''ll go back
with freedom and power...

1033
02:05:36,990 --> 02:05:40,990
and then people can support
Dündar Bey if they want...

1034
02:05:42,050 --> 02:05:45,010
or they can start fighting with me.

1035
02:05:52,250 --> 02:05:56,250
- Give me your blessings.
- I will.

1036
02:06:20,880 --> 02:06:24,440
Osman left with his Alps.

1037
02:06:24,550 --> 02:06:27,750
Finally, he got what he deserved.

1038
02:06:27,850 --> 02:06:32,350
Thanks to Allah. We got
rid of his troubles.

1039
02:06:40,550 --> 02:06:43,120
You don't know what you're doing.

1040
02:06:44,450 --> 02:06:48,450
You have focused on your darkness and
you don't see the light of Osman.

1041
02:06:50,290 --> 02:06:52,130
Shame on you.

1042
02:06:52,180 --> 02:06:53,610
Batur!

1043
02:06:56,520 --> 02:06:58,390
Where are you going?

1044
02:06:58,940 --> 02:07:01,520
I can't stay in this tent.

1045
02:07:01,580 --> 02:07:03,750
What are you saying, son?

1046
02:07:04,000 --> 02:07:06,860
Can your hear what you've just said?

1047
02:07:07,060 --> 02:07:09,380
My place is somewhere else now.

1048
02:07:09,640 --> 02:07:13,100
Osman's exile opened my eyes.

1049
02:07:20,570 --> 02:07:22,610
Give me your blessings, mother.

1050
02:07:28,640 --> 02:07:31,150
- Son... Brother.
- Let him go!

1051
02:07:31,890 --> 02:07:35,300
He can go to hell.

1052
02:07:35,820 --> 02:07:38,990
Will you let him go, Dündar Bey?

1053
02:07:39,320 --> 02:07:45,460
If we'll suppurate, we'll start it
with our children.

1054
02:07:51,570 --> 02:07:53,090
From now on...

1055
02:07:53,630 --> 02:07:56,630
I don't have a child named Batur.

1056
02:08:01,270 --> 02:08:02,700
I don't.

1057
02:08:53,970 --> 02:08:58,940
- Your son is gone! Your son!
- I don't have a son named Batur.

1058
02:09:01,900 --> 02:09:03,360
Saltuk!

1059
02:09:08,090 --> 02:09:09,410
Yes, my Bey.

1060
02:09:09,590 --> 02:09:13,320
Go to Bahadır. I forgave him.

1061
02:09:13,350 --> 02:09:17,970
He should return. He should be
with me on these hard days.

1062
02:09:19,560 --> 02:09:21,430
Your command, my Bey.

1063
02:09:25,540 --> 02:09:31,370
After all these problems, will
we deal with Batur?

1064
02:09:39,370 --> 02:09:44,720
Your son and you debased me.

1065
02:09:46,220 --> 02:09:51,880
I wish I couldn't send Bahadır
and his mother.

1066
02:10:02,580 --> 02:10:06,580
Our tent won't support Dündar Bey anymore.

1067
02:10:07,670 --> 02:10:13,960
It's our duty to protect Kayıs reputation
and make life unbearable for Mongols.

1068
02:10:16,350 --> 02:10:19,850
It's our duty, my Bey.

1069
02:10:20,340 --> 02:10:23,480
What about Osman Bey? He was your friend.

1070
02:10:26,570 --> 02:10:29,120
Osman Bey and I splitted.

1071
02:10:33,140 --> 02:10:36,120
We're alone from now on.

1072
02:10:45,800 --> 02:10:47,960
Can I come in, Samsa Bey?

1073
02:11:23,270 --> 02:11:26,960
I don't even have a word for those
who hide secrets from his friend.

1074
02:11:33,120 --> 02:11:38,020
That secret made us free, Samsa Bey.

1075
02:11:40,390 --> 02:11:43,950
Mongols made us their slaves.

1076
02:11:44,170 --> 02:11:50,480
And you came with an idea that you
don't even say where you've got it from.

1077
02:11:51,570 --> 02:11:55,200
Now that you want something else?

1078
02:11:56,130 --> 02:11:58,550
My secret is a secret, Sergeant Samsa.

1079
02:11:58,950 --> 02:12:01,080
There's nothing else.

1080
02:12:04,250 --> 02:12:06,450
Your secret is a secret.

1081
02:12:09,230 --> 02:12:10,450
Good.

1082
02:12:11,390 --> 02:12:15,250
Are there any other
secrets you hide? Tell me.

1083
02:12:18,020 --> 02:12:20,700
Is this how a friendship is like?

1084
02:12:21,230 --> 02:12:24,240
How can I trust you now?

1085
02:12:25,720 --> 02:12:29,000
How can I send my Alps to death?

1086
02:12:30,600 --> 02:12:34,740
If there's a secret, there
won't be a belief, Osman Bey.

1087
02:12:35,550 --> 02:12:37,550
You're going too far, Sergeant Samsa.

1088
02:12:38,430 --> 02:12:40,710
You're a hero, Osman Bey.

1089
02:12:40,910 --> 02:12:42,700
You're great, Osman Bey.

1090
02:12:43,410 --> 02:12:45,170
You're brave, Osman Bey.

1091
02:12:45,450 --> 02:12:47,680
But you're novice.

1092
02:12:51,000 --> 02:12:54,800
- Pull yourself together, Sergeant Samsa!
- You're novice.

1093
02:12:55,640 --> 02:12:58,230
We've been friends but...

1094
02:12:58,230 --> 02:13:01,400
you're being cruel!

1095
02:13:01,500 --> 02:13:04,460
You don't have a place in this
tent, novice Osman!

1096
02:13:47,430 --> 02:13:49,980
That's not a friendship, Osman!

1097
02:13:52,140 --> 02:13:54,560
- Boran.
- Konur, stop.

1098
02:13:54,750 --> 02:13:58,120
- Boran, should we go inside?
- Stop, brother.

1099
02:13:58,250 --> 02:14:02,250
We'll be harmed.

1100
02:14:02,680 --> 02:14:04,050
Let's wait.

1101
02:14:18,720 --> 02:14:20,990
Is that all, Sergeant Samsa?

1102
02:14:47,250 --> 02:14:49,480
You should've not done that to me.

1103
02:14:50,500 --> 02:14:56,040
It's hard to establish a state with
people who rebel and run away.

1104
02:14:57,860 --> 02:15:01,790
Everyone will rebel if I give a chance to you.

1105
02:15:02,430 --> 02:15:05,070
You shouldn't rebel me.

1106
02:15:05,830 --> 02:15:10,010
I ran out of patience.

1107
02:15:28,220 --> 02:15:37,530
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com